  "Content": {
    "Html": "<p class=\"p1\">Ground ginger and ginger tea are put to the test for blood sugar control.</p>\n<p class=\"p1\">In a case report of the “successful management of type 2 diabetes with lifestyle intervention,” a 45-year-old man took responsibility for his health into his own hands and sought to <a class=\"Hyperlink SCXW35101630 BCX0\" href=\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/26098477\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><span class=\"TextRun Underlined SCXW35101630 BCX0\" lang=\"EN-US\" xml:lang=\"EN-US\" data-contrast=\"none\"><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW35101630 BCX0\" data-ccp-charstyle=\"Hyperlink.0\" data-ccp-charstyle-defn=\"{&#34;ObjectId&#34;:&#34;d837e8d8-4207-4658-b414-b2f1da324180|53&#34;,&#34;ClassId&#34;:1073872969,&#34;Properties&#34;:[469775450,&#34;Hyperlink.0&#34;,201340122,&#34;1&#34;,134233614,&#34;true&#34;,469778129,&#34;Hyperlink0&#34;,335572020,&#34;1&#34;,134224902,&#34;true&#34;,201334293,&#34;0&#34;,335551500,&#34;5287936&#34;,469778324,&#34;Hyperlink&#34;]}\">defeat</span></span></a> his disease and get off the meds by eating foods purported to be anti-diabetic, as you can see <span class=\"notion-enable-hover\" data-token-index=\"0\">below and </span>at 0:20 in my video <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/flashback-friday-is-ginger-beneficial-in-a-diabetic-diet/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Flashback Friday: Is Ginger Beneficial in a Diabetic Diet?</strong></a>. How strong is the evidence for ginger?</p>\n<p><img decoding=\"async\" class=\"aligncenter size-full wp-image-93049\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/0-20.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1920\" height=\"1080\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/0-20.png 1920w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/0-20-960x540.png 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/0-20-1024x576.png 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/0-20-768x432.png 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/0-20-1536x864.png 1536w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/0-20-480x270.png 480w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/0-20-1200x675.png 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/0-20-720x405.png 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/0-20-540x304.png 540w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1920px) 100vw, 1920px\"/></p>\n<p class=\"p1\">“Diabetes is <a class=\"Hyperlink SCXW90535123 BCX0\" href=\"https://www.hindawi.com/journals/njos/2014/674684/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><span class=\"TextRun Underlined SCXW90535123 BCX0\" lang=\"EN-US\" xml:lang=\"EN-US\" data-contrast=\"none\"><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW90535123 BCX0\" data-ccp-charstyle=\"Hyperlink.0\" data-ccp-charstyle-defn=\"{&#34;ObjectId&#34;:&#34;d837e8d8-4207-4658-b414-b2f1da324180|53&#34;,&#34;ClassId&#34;:1073872969,&#34;Properties&#34;:[469775450,&#34;Hyperlink.0&#34;,201340122,&#34;1&#34;,134233614,&#34;true&#34;,469778129,&#34;Hyperlink0&#34;,335572020,&#34;1&#34;,134224902,&#34;true&#34;,201334293,&#34;0&#34;,335551500,&#34;5287936&#34;,469778324,&#34;Hyperlink&#34;]}\">reaching</span></span></a> pandemic levels…and requires safe, affordable, and effective therapies.” So, what about ginger’s “potential in prevention and treatment”? As you can see <span class=\"notion-enable-hover\" data-token-index=\"0\">in the graph below and </span>at 0:37 in my <strong><a class=\"Hyperlink SCXW90535123 BCX0\" href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/is-ginger-beneficial-in-a-diabetic-diet/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><span class=\"TextRun Underlined MacChromeBold SCXW90535123 BCX0\" lang=\"EN-US\" xml:lang=\"EN-US\" data-contrast=\"none\"><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW90535123 BCX0\" data-ccp-charstyle=\"Hyperlink\">video</span></span></a></strong>, in a petri dish, increasing exposure to ginger compounds <a class=\"Hyperlink SCXW90535123 BCX0\" href=\"https://www.hindawi.com/journals/njos/2014/674684/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><span class=\"TextRun Underlined SCXW90535123 BCX0\" lang=\"IT-IT\" xml:lang=\"IT-IT\" data-contrast=\"none\"><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW90535123 BCX0\" data-ccp-charstyle=\"Hyperlink.0\">improves</span></span></a> blood sugar uptake of muscle cells almost as much as the popular diabetes drug metformin. </p>\n<p><img decoding=\"async\" class=\"aligncenter size-full wp-image-93051\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/0-37.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1920\" height=\"1080\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/0-37.png 1920w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/0-37-960x540.png 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/0-37-1024x576.png 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/0-37-768x432.png 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/0-37-1536x864.png 1536w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/0-37-480x270.png 480w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/0-37-1200x675.png 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/0-37-720x405.png 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/0-37-540x304.png 540w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1920px) 100vw, 1920px\"/></p>\n<p>And, in rats, ginger might <a class=\"Hyperlink SCXW90535123 BCX0\" href=\"http://www.jocpr.com/abstract/evaluation-of-anti-hyperglycaemic-activity-of-zingiber-officinaleginger-in-albino-rats-992.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><span class=\"TextRun Underlined SCXW90535123 BCX0\" lang=\"EN-US\" xml:lang=\"EN-US\" data-contrast=\"none\"><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW90535123 BCX0\" data-ccp-charstyle=\"Hyperlink.0\">work</span></span></a> even better than metformin, but weight and blood sugar reduction observed in rodent models “does not <a class=\"Hyperlink SCXW90535123 BCX0\" href=\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/27093610\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><span class=\"TextRun Underlined SCXW90535123 BCX0\" lang=\"DE-DE\" xml:lang=\"DE-DE\" data-contrast=\"none\"><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW90535123 BCX0\" data-ccp-charstyle=\"Hyperlink.0\">translate</span></span></a> to humans.” As you can see <span class=\"notion-enable-hover\" data-token-index=\"0\">in the graph below and </span>at 0:59 in my <strong><a class=\"Hyperlink SCXW90535123 BCX0\" href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/is-ginger-beneficial-in-a-diabetic-diet/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><span class=\"TextRun Underlined MacChromeBold SCXW90535123 BCX0\" lang=\"EN-US\" xml:lang=\"EN-US\" data-contrast=\"none\"><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW90535123 BCX0\" data-ccp-charstyle=\"Hyperlink\">video</span></span></a></strong><span class=\"TextRun SCXW90535123 BCX0\" lang=\"EN-US\" xml:lang=\"EN-US\" data-contrast=\"none\"><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW90535123 BCX0\" data-ccp-parastyle=\"Body\">, </span></span>a combination of nutraceuticals caused mice to lose 30 percent of their body weight in one month, but what about people? Researchers found no benefit compared to placebo. You don’t really know if something works in humans until you put it to the test.</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"aligncenter size-full wp-image-93053\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/0-59.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1920\" height=\"1080\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/0-59.png 1920w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/0-59-960x540.png 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/0-59-1024x576.png 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/0-59-768x432.png 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/0-59-1536x864.png 1536w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/0-59-480x270.png 480w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/0-59-1200x675.png 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/0-59-720x405.png 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/0-59-540x304.png 540w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1920px) 100vw, 1920px\"/></p>\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"TextRun SCXW148681678 BCX0\" lang=\"EN-US\" xml:lang=\"EN-US\" data-contrast=\"none\"><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW148681678 BCX0\" data-ccp-parastyle=\"Body\" data-ccp-parastyle-defn=\"{&#34;ObjectId&#34;:&#34;d837e8d8-4207-4658-b414-b2f1da324180|52&#34;,&#34;ClassId&#34;:1073872969,&#34;Properties&#34;:[469775450,&#34;Body&#34;,201340122,&#34;2&#34;,134233614,&#34;true&#34;,469778129,&#34;Body&#34;,335572020,&#34;1&#34;,469777841,&#34;Helvetica Neue&#34;,469777842,&#34;Helvetica Neue&#34;,469777843,&#34;Helvetica Neue&#34;,469777844,&#34;Helvetica Neue&#34;,469769226,&#34;Helvetica Neue&#34;,335551500,&#34;0&#34;,268442635,&#34;22&#34;]}\">W</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW148681678 BCX0\" data-ccp-parastyle=\"Body\">hen researchers fed people refined white</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW148681678 BCX0\" data-ccp-parastyle=\"Body\">–</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW148681678 BCX0\" data-ccp-parastyle=\"Body\">flour bread with a cup of water, their blood sugars </span></span><a class=\"Hyperlink SCXW148681678 BCX0\" href=\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/24199490\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><span class=\"TextRun Underlined SCXW148681678 BCX0\" lang=\"EN-US\" xml:lang=\"EN-US\" data-contrast=\"none\"><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW148681678 BCX0\" data-ccp-charstyle=\"Hyperlink.0\" data-ccp-charstyle-defn=\"{&#34;ObjectId&#34;:&#34;d837e8d8-4207-4658-b414-b2f1da324180|53&#34;,&#34;ClassId&#34;:1073872969,&#34;Properties&#34;:[469775450,&#34;Hyperlink.0&#34;,201340122,&#34;1&#34;,134233614,&#34;true&#34;,469778129,&#34;Hyperlink0&#34;,335572020,&#34;1&#34;,134224902,&#34;true&#34;,201334293,&#34;0&#34;,335551500,&#34;5287936&#34;,469778324,&#34;Hyperlink&#34;]}\">rose</span></span></a><span class=\"TextRun SCXW148681678 BCX0\" lang=\"EN-US\" xml:lang=\"EN-US\" data-contrast=\"none\"><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW148681678 BCX0\" data-ccp-parastyle=\"Body\"> over the next two hours. But</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW148681678 BCX0\" data-ccp-parastyle=\"Body\">,</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW148681678 BCX0\" data-ccp-parastyle=\"Body\"> when they drank some unsweetened green tea </span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW148681678 BCX0\" data-ccp-parastyle=\"Body\">with</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW148681678 BCX0\" data-ccp-parastyle=\"Body\"> that white bread instead</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW148681678 BCX0\" data-ccp-parastyle=\"Body\"> of plain water</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW148681678 BCX0\" data-ccp-parastyle=\"Body\">, there was less of a blood sugar spike. </span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW148681678 BCX0\" data-ccp-parastyle=\"Body\">T</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW148681678 BCX0\" data-ccp-parastyle=\"Body\">he same with cinnamon tea </span><span class=\"NormalTextRun AdvancedProofingIssueV2Themed SCXW148681678 BCX0\" data-ccp-parastyle=\"Body\">and </span><span class=\"NormalTextRun AdvancedProofingIssueV2Themed SCXW148681678 BCX0\" data-ccp-parastyle=\"Body\">also</span> <span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW148681678 BCX0\" data-ccp-parastyle=\"Body\">with ginger tea made by mixing a tablespoon of grated fresh ginger in</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW148681678 BCX0\" data-ccp-parastyle=\"Body\">to</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW148681678 BCX0\" data-ccp-parastyle=\"Body\"> a cup of hot water. </span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW148681678 BCX0\" data-ccp-parastyle=\"Body\">You can see this below and at 1:17 in </span><span class=\"NormalTextRun ContextualSpellingAndGrammarErrorV2Themed SCXW148681678 BCX0\" data-ccp-parastyle=\"Body\">my</span> </span><a class=\"Hyperlink SCXW148681678 BCX0\" href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/is-ginger-beneficial-in-a-diabetic-diet/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><span class=\"TextRun Underlined MacChromeBold SCXW148681678 BCX0\" lang=\"EN-US\" xml:lang=\"EN-US\" data-contrast=\"none\"><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW148681678 BCX0\" data-ccp-charstyle=\"Hyperlink\"><strong>video</strong></span></span></a><span class=\"TextRun SCXW148681678 BCX0\" lang=\"EN-US\" xml:lang=\"EN-US\" data-contrast=\"none\"><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW148681678 BCX0\" data-ccp-parastyle=\"Body\">. The study subjects </span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW148681678 BCX0\" data-ccp-parastyle=\"Body\">were </span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW148681678 BCX0\" data-ccp-parastyle=\"Body\">all </span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW148681678 BCX0\" data-ccp-parastyle=\"Body\">healthy, </span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW148681678 BCX0\" data-ccp-parastyle=\"Body\">though</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW148681678 BCX0\" data-ccp-parastyle=\"Body\">. What about the effects of ginger in </span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW148681678 BCX0\" data-ccp-parastyle=\"Body\">people with </span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW148681678 BCX0\" data-ccp-parastyle=\"Body\">diabet</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW148681678 BCX0\" data-ccp-parastyle=\"Body\">es</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW148681678 BCX0\" data-ccp-parastyle=\"Body\">?</span></span><span class=\"EOP SCXW148681678 BCX0\" data-ccp-props=\"{}\"> </span></p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"aligncenter size-full wp-image-93055\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/1-17.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1920\" height=\"1080\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/1-17.png 1920w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/1-17-960x540.png 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/1-17-1024x576.png 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/1-17-768x432.png 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/1-17-1536x864.png 1536w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/1-17-480x270.png 480w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/1-17-1200x675.png 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/1-17-720x405.png 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/1-17-540x304.png 540w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1920px) 100vw, 1920px\"/></p>\n<p><span data-contrast=\"none\">In the first study of its kind, diabetics were </span><a href=\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/23496212\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span data-contrast=\"none\">randomized</span></a><span data-contrast=\"none\"> to take a teaspoon of ground ginger a day for two months. It was hidden in pill form, so the researchers could compare results with subjects taking identical-looking sugar pill placebos. The result? Ginger supplementation<span class=\"TextRun Underlined SCXW229622001 BCX0\" lang=\"EN-US\" xml:lang=\"EN-US\" data-contrast=\"none\"><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW229622001 BCX0\" data-ccp-charstyle=\"Hyperlink.0\" data-ccp-charstyle-defn=\"{&#34;ObjectId&#34;:&#34;d837e8d8-4207-4658-b414-b2f1da324180|53&#34;,&#34;ClassId&#34;:1073872969,&#34;Properties&#34;:[469775450,&#34;Hyperlink.0&#34;,201340122,&#34;1&#34;,134233614,&#34;true&#34;,469778129,&#34;Hyperlink0&#34;,335572020,&#34;1&#34;,134224902,&#34;true&#34;,201334293,&#34;0&#34;,335551500,&#34;5287936&#34;,469778324,&#34;Hyperlink&#34;]}\"> <span class=\"TextRun Underlined SCXW65936432 BCX0\" lang=\"EN-US\" xml:lang=\"EN-US\" data-contrast=\"none\"><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW65936432 BCX0\" data-ccp-charstyle=\"Hyperlink.0\">decreased</span></span><span class=\"TextRun Underlined SCXW49384513 BCX0\" lang=\"EN-US\" xml:lang=\"EN-US\" data-contrast=\"none\"><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW49384513 BCX0\" data-ccp-charstyle=\"Hyperlink.0\"> </span></span></span></span></span><span data-contrast=\"none\">the levels of insulin, which is a good thing, as well as lowered levels of triglycerides and LDL cholesterol, but without a significant effect on blood sugars. Now, heart disease is the leading killer of diabetics, so a 13 percent drop in bad LDL cholesterol would be reason enough to shell out the nickel a day it would cost to add that much ginger to your diet, but it would have been nice to also see an improvement in blood sugar control. There was that drop in insulin levels, which suggests improved insulin sensitivity, and a significant drop in insulin resistance. Is it possible the researchers just didn’t give the ginger enough time to work? That study gave it two months, but what giving three months?</span><span data-ccp-props=\"{}\"> </span></p>\n<p><span data-contrast=\"none\">Researchers </span><a href=\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/24490949\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span data-contrast=\"none\">gave</span></a><span data-contrast=\"none\"> subjects even less ginger, just 1.6 grams, less than a teaspoon a day, but did so for 12 weeks, and</span><span data-contrast=\"none\"> ginger </span><span data-contrast=\"none\">did in fact </span><a href=\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/24490949\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span data-contrast=\"none\">reduce</span></a><span data-contrast=\"none\"> blood sugar levels, as well as decrease inflammation, cutting C-reactive protein levels in half.</span><span data-ccp-props=\"{}\"> </span></p>\n<p><span data-contrast=\"none\">What about </span><a href=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/24559810/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span data-contrast=\"none\">scaling</span></a><span data-contrast=\"none\"> down to just eight weeks, but, this time, using a higher dose—3.0 grams a day, which is about one and a half teaspoons? Researchers </span><span data-contrast=\"none\">found</span><span data-contrast=\"none\"> a significant</span><span data-contrast=\"none\"> decrease in fasting blood sugars and long-term blood sugar control in the ginger group, “thereby showing the effect of ginger in </span><span data-contrast=\"none\">controlling</span><span data-contrast=\"none\"> diabetes.” </span><span data-contrast=\"none\">In fact, the placebo group continued to get worse, while the ginger group got better, as you can see below and at 3:14 in my </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/is-ginger-beneficial-in-a-diabetic-diet/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><b><span data-contrast=\"none\">video</span></b></a><span data-contrast=\"none\">.</span><span data-ccp-props=\"{}\"> </span></p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"aligncenter size-full wp-image-93057\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/3-14.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1920\" height=\"1080\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/3-14.png 1920w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/3-14-960x540.png 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/3-14-1024x576.png 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/3-14-768x432.png 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/3-14-1536x864.png 1536w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/3-14-480x270.png 480w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/3-14-1200x675.png 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/3-14-720x405.png 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/3-14-540x304.png 540w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1920px) 100vw, 1920px\"/></p>\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"TextRun SCXW128561631 BCX0\" lang=\"EN-US\" xml:lang=\"EN-US\" data-contrast=\"none\"><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW128561631 BCX0\" data-ccp-parastyle=\"Body\" data-ccp-parastyle-defn=\"{&#34;ObjectId&#34;:&#34;d837e8d8-4207-4658-b414-b2f1da324180|52&#34;,&#34;ClassId&#34;:1073872969,&#34;Properties&#34;:[469775450,&#34;Body&#34;,201340122,&#34;2&#34;,134233614,&#34;true&#34;,469778129,&#34;Body&#34;,335572020,&#34;1&#34;,469777841,&#34;Helvetica Neue&#34;,469777842,&#34;Helvetica Neue&#34;,469777843,&#34;Helvetica Neue&#34;,469777844,&#34;Helvetica Neue&#34;,469769226,&#34;Helvetica Neue&#34;,335551500,&#34;0&#34;,268442635,&#34;22&#34;]}\">Similarly, researchers </span></span><a class=\"Hyperlink SCXW128561631 BCX0\" href=\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/25561919\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><span class=\"TextRun Underlined SCXW128561631 BCX0\" lang=\"EN-US\" xml:lang=\"EN-US\" data-contrast=\"none\"><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW128561631 BCX0\" data-ccp-charstyle=\"Hyperlink.0\" data-ccp-charstyle-defn=\"{&#34;ObjectId&#34;:&#34;d837e8d8-4207-4658-b414-b2f1da324180|53&#34;,&#34;ClassId&#34;:1073872969,&#34;Properties&#34;:[469775450,&#34;Hyperlink.0&#34;,201340122,&#34;1&#34;,134233614,&#34;true&#34;,469778129,&#34;Hyperlink0&#34;,335572020,&#34;1&#34;,134224902,&#34;true&#34;,201334293,&#34;0&#34;,335551500,&#34;5287936&#34;,469778324,&#34;Hyperlink&#34;]}\">saw</span></span></a><span class=\"TextRun SCXW128561631 BCX0\" lang=\"EN-US\" xml:lang=\"EN-US\" data-contrast=\"none\"><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW128561631 BCX0\" data-ccp-parastyle=\"Body\"> amazing results in a randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled study with a teaspoon a day for </span><span class=\"NormalTextRun AdvancedProofingIssueV2Themed SCXW128561631 BCX0\" data-ccp-parastyle=\"Body\">12 weeks</span> <span class=\"NormalTextRun AdvancedProofingIssueV2Themed SCXW128561631 BCX0\" data-ccp-parastyle=\"Body\">a</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun AdvancedProofingIssueV2Themed SCXW128561631 BCX0\" data-ccp-parastyle=\"Body\">nd also</span> <span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW128561631 BCX0\" data-ccp-parastyle=\"Body\">recorded</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW128561631 BCX0\" data-ccp-parastyle=\"Body\"> improvements </span></span><a class=\"Hyperlink SCXW128561631 BCX0\" href=\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/25719344\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><span class=\"TextRun Underlined SCXW128561631 BCX0\" lang=\"EN-US\" xml:lang=\"EN-US\" data-contrast=\"none\"><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW128561631 BCX0\" data-ccp-charstyle=\"Hyperlink.0\">using</span></span></a><span class=\"TextRun SCXW128561631 BCX0\" lang=\"EN-US\" xml:lang=\"EN-US\" data-contrast=\"none\"><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW128561631 BCX0\" data-ccp-parastyle=\"Body\"> a teaspoon and a half, where </span><span class=\"NormalTextRun AdvancedProofingIssueV2Themed SCXW128561631 BCX0\" data-ccp-parastyle=\"Body\">all </span><span class=\"NormalTextRun AdvancedProofingIssueV2Themed SCXW128561631 BCX0\" data-ccp-parastyle=\"Body\">of</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW128561631 BCX0\" data-ccp-parastyle=\"Body\"> the participants in the ginger group </span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW128561631 BCX0\" data-ccp-parastyle=\"Body\">were better and all </span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW128561631 BCX0\" data-ccp-parastyle=\"Body\">of those </span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW128561631 BCX0\" data-ccp-parastyle=\"Body\">in the non-ginger group</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW128561631 BCX0\" data-ccp-parastyle=\"Body\"> were worse</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW128561631 BCX0\" data-ccp-parastyle=\"Body\">, as you can see below and at 3:27 in </span><span class=\"NormalTextRun ContextualSpellingAndGrammarErrorV2Themed SCXW128561631 BCX0\" data-ccp-parastyle=\"Body\">my</span> </span><strong><a class=\"Hyperlink SCXW128561631 BCX0\" href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/is-ginger-beneficial-in-a-diabetic-diet/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><span class=\"TextRun Underlined MacChromeBold SCXW128561631 BCX0\" lang=\"EN-US\" xml:lang=\"EN-US\" data-contrast=\"none\"><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW128561631 BCX0\" data-ccp-charstyle=\"Hyperlink\">video</span></span></a></strong><span class=\"TextRun SCXW128561631 BCX0\" lang=\"EN-US\" xml:lang=\"EN-US\" data-contrast=\"none\"><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW128561631 BCX0\" data-ccp-parastyle=\"Body\">.</span></span><span class=\"EOP SCXW128561631 BCX0\" data-ccp-props=\"{}\"> </span></p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"aligncenter size-full wp-image-93059\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/3-27.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1920\" height=\"1080\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/3-27.png 1920w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/3-27-960x540.png 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/3-27-1024x576.png 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/3-27-768x432.png 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/3-27-1536x864.png 1536w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/3-27-480x270.png 480w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/3-27-1200x675.png 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/3-27-720x405.png 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/05/3-27-540x304.png 540w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1920px) 100vw, 1920px\"/></p>\n<p><span data-contrast=\"none\">So much </span><span data-contrast=\"none\">significant</span><span data-contrast=\"none\"> difference, just because of a small amount of an inexpensive, safe, simple, and side-effect-free spice. If you put together all of the studies, “the combined data clearly </span><a href=\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S2352618115000086\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span data-contrast=\"none\">demonstrated</span></a><span data-contrast=\"none\">”</span><span data-contrast=\"none\"> that ginger can lower blood sugar levels and improve long-term blood sugar control—and do so at a totally manageable dose. You could just stir a teaspoon of ginger powder into a cup of hot water and drink it. How easy is that? So, “overall…‘</span><a href=\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0308814616313516\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span data-contrast=\"none\">adding</span></a><span data-contrast=\"none\"> [a] little spice to our life’ may serve as a delicious and sensible way to maintain a healthy body.”</span><span data-ccp-props=\"{}\"> </span></p>\n<p>If one plant can do all of this, can you imagine if your whole diet was centered around plants?</p>\n<p class=\"p1\">Here’s a video to draw you in to the dozens more I have on diabetes, one of our leading killers:<strong> <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/how-not-to-die-from-diabetes/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">How Not to Die from Diabetes</a></strong>.</p>"
